Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Thank you for the KIP. Overall, the proposal looks good to me.

I am adding some additional comments here:

1. What type of constraints do we want to add on static configuration? I am
assuming we should probably define some sane lower limit so that basic
replication (empty fetch requests) can still proceed normally. I am
suggesting this because users may mis-configure this and block simple fetch
requests which act as "heartbeat" in Kafka. This will lead to clusters
becoming unstable in weird ways and would be very hard to debug.

2. There is a problem with existing broker-level throttling that it will
throttle reserved topics as well (please correct me if I am wrong here).
This is because the reserved topics (such as __metadata, __consumer_offsets
etc.) are treated the same as regular topics from a throttling perspective.
Having a static configuration would increase the probability of landing in
a situation where the cluster becomes unstable since replication for
reserved topics is getting throttled. This is not a blocker for this KIP
because this is not a new risk, it already exists with dynamic
configuration, but perhaps worth calling out as a risk in our documentation
since the probability of risk will increase now. This is also the reason I
do not want users to set throttling below a certain threshold (and hence,
introduce a lower bound).

--=20
Divij Vaidya



