    Resolution: Abandoned

> Incremental Batch Processing for Kafka Streams
> ----------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-4437
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-4437
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: New Feature
>          Components: streams
>            Reporter: Matthias J. Sax
>            Priority: Major
>
> We want to add an =E2=80=9Cauto stop=E2=80=9D feature that terminate a st=
ream application when it has processed all the data that was newly availabl=
e at the time the application started (to at current end-of-log, i.e., curr=
ent high watermark). This allows to chop the (infinite) log into finite chu=
nks where each run for the application processes one chunk. This feature al=
lows for incremental batch-like processing; think "start-process-stop-resta=
rt-process-stop-..."
> For details see KIP-95: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA=
/KIP-95%3A+Incremental+Batch+Processing+for+Kafka+Streams



