Hello forks,

Kafka 4.0 is a major release that introduces significant changes. We =
have deprecated outdated APIs and=20
established a new baseline version of 2.1 as defined in KIP-896. While =
there has been extensive discussion=20
in related PRs regarding broker-client compatibility, the client upgrade =
and migration paths have not been explicitly defined.=20
For the client module, the current tentative baseline is version 2.0, =
which was already discussed in PR[1]. A new KIP will be=20
introduced to further clarify this.
However, what I=E2=80=99m particularly curious about is why KIP-896 set =
the baseline version to 2.1 instead of 2.0.
I would appreciate any insights on this.

[1]Discussion PR =
<https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/18193#issuecomment-2572283545>

Best regards,
Jiunn-Yang=

