Jonah Hooper created KAFKA-18442:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Downgrades to 3.3.2 will fail from versions 3.6.0 and=
 above
                 Key: KAFKA-18442
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18442
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Jonah Hooper


Downgrading from 3.6.x and above to 3.3.x will fail with the following erro=
r:
{code:java}
 kafka.common.InconsistentBrokerMetadataException: BrokerMetadata is not co=
nsistent across log.dirs. This could happen if multiple brokers shared a lo=
g directory (log.dirs) or partial data was manually copied from another bro=
ker. Found:- /mnt/kafka/kafka-metadata-logs -> {node.id=3D1, directory.id=
=3DItAoMTrsidYVfoRnX3gsAA, version=3D1, cluster.id=3DI2eXt9rvSnyhct8BYmW6-w=
}- /mnt/kafka/kafka-data-logs-2 -> {node.id=3D1, directory.id=3DMiQDnIX6WuY=
L0NdMaLOsRQ, version=3D1, cluster.id=3DI2eXt9rvSnyhct8BYmW6-w}- /mnt/kafka/=
kafka-data-logs-1 -> {node.id=3D1, directory.id=3DF1m5lsdOIsGtTpTYT0Ao9g, v=
ersion=3D1, cluster.id=3DI2eXt9rvSnyhct8BYmW6-w}
=09at kafka.server.BrokerMetadataCheckpoint$.getBrokerMetadataAndOfflineDir=
s(BrokerMetadataCheckpoint.scala:194)=09at kafka.server.KafkaRaftServer$.in=
itializeLogDirs(KafkaRaftServer.scala:184)=09at kafka.server.KafkaRaftServe=
r.<init>(KafkaRaftServer.scala:61)=09at kafka.Kafka$.buildServer(Kafka.scal=
a:79)=09at kafka.Kafka$.main(Kafka.scala:87)=09at kafka.Kafka.main(Kafka.sc=
ala){code}
=C2=A0

This is only broken in 3.3.2 version of Kafka=C2=A0[BrokerMetatadataCheckpo=
int.scala|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/c9c03dd7ef9ff4edf2596e905cab=
ececc72a9e9d/core/src/main/scala/kafka/server/BrokerMetadataCheckpoint.scal=
a#L186]. In 3.3.2 kafka loads information about metadata directories via=C2=
=A0{{metadata.properties}}=C2=A0files and expects that the properties are d=
uplicated for all log directories. We crash with a fatal error if they are =
non-duplicate which at that time would mean that another instance of kafka =
was using the same log directories.

In [#14291|https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/14291] we dropped the requi=
rement that the {{metadata.properties}}=C2=A0files is duplicate in each dir=
ectory since they will now contain a non-unique=C2=A0{{directory.id}}=C2=A0=
field for each dir. This has no effect on versions of kafka running=C2=A0{{=
kraft}} mode, >=3D 3.4.x (they care only about uniqueness of node.id and cl=
uster.id) but does affect 3.3.2 and lower (than [#9967|[https://github.com/=
apache/kafka/pull/9967])] since it expects every {{metadata.properties}} fi=
le to be the same.



