Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-18464) Empty Abort Transaction can fence
 producer incorrectly with Transactions V2
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Justine Olshan created KAFKA-18464:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Empty Abort Transaction can fence producer incorrectl=
y with Transactions V2
                 Key: KAFKA-18464
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18464
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 4.0.0
            Reporter: Justine Olshan
            Assignee: Justine Olshan


Consider the following scenario using transactions V2.

Producer writes a transaction and commits.=C2=A0
Producer starts the next transaction and tries to add a partition but gets =
an non-retriable error. Because the application doesn't know whether the pa=
rtition was added/records written the producer aborts. In the case where th=
e partition was not added, and the previous transaction was still in Prepar=
eCommit state, we self-fence.=C2=A0

This is because the epoch of the current state =3D=3D incoming request epoc=
h and the PrepareCommit state currently only allows for retries where the r=
equest epoch is -1 the current epoch.=C2=A0

Instead of hitting this, we should just return the concurrent transactions =
error when we have pending state and do the epoch check second. In this sce=
nario, we will complete commit before proceeding to the empty abort.=C2=A0



