Konstantin Morozov created KAFKA-18496:
------------------------------------------

             Summary: Using ACL and StandardAuthorizer with PLAINTEXT
                 Key: KAFKA-18496
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18496
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Konstantin Morozov
         Attachments: NonStandardAuthorizer.java

It is not intended, but possible to use ACL and StandardAuthorizer with PLAINTEXT. As an example I've created an class, extending StandardAuthorizer that avoids limitations of PrincipalBuilder of PLAINTEXT.


But there are several cases, when StandardAuthorizer::authorize methods invokes with empty List<Action> actions, e.g. when AuthHelper::filterByAuthorized invoked for DESCRIBE AclOperation with empth resouces list (it is possible in brocker registration process and in add ACL). As a result, context of security request in Authorizer is lost, and method StandardAuthorizer::authorize dont knows which action to authorise.


My w/a creates fake principal with fake ResourcePattern with type LITERAL, because ANY is not allowed in constructor. I suggest add check if resource is empty and pass to Authorizer some valid placeholder.



